==Overview==
<tabber> 
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High combo potential, all moves can be combined easily.
* All moves are AoE moves, making it a great fruit to grind with if the user can combine the high-damage abilities together with the summoned spirits.
* Extremely high damage, easy to pressure enemies while in a PvP, since a small mistake can result in their health being depleted rapidly.
* Extremely versatile. With the help of the buddies, the user can use a lot of the perks that the game has to offer: stun, healing, movement speed, DoT, AoE, and knockback.
* Can be used for hybrid builds.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* The Buddies cannot be harmed, but they vanish after a few seconds. The range of their parkside is also not affected by the players' distance from them. For example, if the user has a healing spirit, it will still heal them even if they are far away.
* The healing/speed spirits allow the user to easily switch their play style from being aggressive to being passive.
* Good for grinding
* The Cursed Tree has auto-aim.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Stuns enemies for a long time.
* Has a big hitbox.
* Useful for combo finishers.
* Deals more damage when attacking more enemies.
* Has hit-scan.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Provides DoT [burning], temporarily making it disable [[Instinct]] for a while in PvP.
* High range (when held) and high damage, combining well into {{Ability|V}}.
* The animation creates an explosion, making it difficult for the enemy to react in time.
* Extremely high damage if landed, more than most [V] attacks.

|{{Ability|C}}
* Long stun and large [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Quick start and low end-lag, making it a good move to "catch" people.

|{{Ability|V}}
* Long stun and large [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
** Even the stun from the beams have extremely big hitboxes, making it good to 'snag' opponents.
* Insanely high & powerful damage, allowing the user to kill enemies with much shorter combos.
* Out-ranges [[Energy Core]] and [[Primordial Reign]], effectively making it un-cancelable.
* Highly recommended to raise mouse sensitivity to make sharp angles easily (the beams are a little slow when turning).

|{{Ability|F}}
* Good for sky camping.
* Moderately Fast.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Extremely high Mastery requirements for all moves, tied with [[Control]] and [[Dragon]] at 350 mastery.
* Moves are considered to be relatively slow.
* Hard to obtain.
* Very punishing to miss abilities as almost all the moves have long endlag.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* The possibility of spawning buddies is random, making it possible for the user to get buddies they do not want (Such as a star instead of a flying pig).
* Toxic Mushroom is nearly useless in PvP, since no one's going to stay inside the fog, and Cursed Tree can be easily avoided by air camping or staying away. Along with that, dashing and running can avoid Toad extremely easily.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Relatively short range, but makes up for it with its huge hitbox.
* High endlag, makes the user vulnerable to attacks if missed.
* Unpredicatable knockback makes it unreliable for combo starting.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Long range has a short wind up before release, relatively short range when tapped.
* Can be [[Instinct]] tricked.

|{{Ability|C}}
* Can be punished if missed. (It is unlikely however, as the [[Area of Effect|AoE]] would freeze enemies had they been so close).

|{{Ability|V}}
* Vulnerable if missed. (Directing the beam’s explosion on the user may help keep enemies away from attacking).

|{{Ability|F}}
* Not recommended for use in pursuit of enemies or as a platform for aerial PvP.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Rarely, Toad may lose its textures, as shown in the image above.
* Both Ra and Shu attack in combination while using {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|V}}.
* '''Cursed Tree''' is the only buddy whose form was not changed during the rework in {{Update|17.3}}.
* Due to the nerf in [[Updates/24|Update 24]] to [[Angel]]'s [[Heavenly Blood|V3 ability]], the healing ability of the stars offers a great alternative for those looking to heal in a pinch. Much like [[Angel]]'s [[Heavenly Blood|V3 ability]], making it ideal in the heat of battle.
* {{Ability|X}} has a visual bug that makes it slightly hard to land from afar, but it is easier to use when aiming under the user's avatar.
* {{Ability|C}} has different sound effects for different targets, slowly scaling with larger opponents. The absolute maximum size is against a [[Sea Beast]], when cast on one, its sound effect is almost akin to the shattering of glass.
* For some reason, the Spirit fruit model/image has the Angel and Demon sides switched.
* Spirit, along with [[Venom]], are the only fruits to retain their original physical fruit models since [[Updates/20|Update 20]].
* Shu is very expressive, but its animation cycle does not start until a few minutes have been spent in the server.
** This is likely to reduce loading.
* The speed buff from the pig buddy only affects run and dash speed, and not the speed of the flight move. Meaning that there is no purpose in trying to use the speed boost and then fly.

